 # Meet Proxy setup
 
+Open Spaces, continue with Google and choose your desktop app. **Copy setup
+prompt**, paste it into the intended chat and press Send. The prepared request
+installs the plugin and configures MCP together. If the host asks, approve that
+action or reload the plugin there. Browser sign-in carries over; an already linked
+installation needs no second Google sign-in.
+
+The private `commonplace-context:` handoff binds that exact native chat and starts
+automatic private collection. Setup confirms registration, received context and
+searchable context separately. Opening an app or copying a prompt is not completion.
+You can start with the context available while more history continues collecting.
+
+Ask normal questions such as “What did we decide about launch?” The assistant
+searches and reads your authorized context through MCP, using its existing model.
+The local folder is optional and is not a prerequisite. Every host still controls
+its own tool permissions. A request timeout does not mean sign-in expired.
+
+For a shared group, ask to create a space and return its invitation link. Ask your
+assistant to join a supplied space invitation to preview and accept it through MCP.
+Joining grants membership only; personal-library sharing stays off until each
+contributor enables their own rules. Queries and approved excerpts appear in
+Messages for all members.
+
+## Existing installation and legacy invitations
+
 Install **meet-proxy** from the **diask5/commonplace-plugin** marketplace, then
 activate it in your existing chat. Keep only your existing alias enabled.
 Ask **“Check Meet Proxy setup”** or use `/meet-proxy:setup`. The read-only
